    "core_content": {
      "parsing_res_list": [
        {
          "block_label": "paragraph_title",
          "block_content": "The Quotient Rule ",
          "block_bbox": [
            137,
            187,
            1493,
            328
          ],
          "block_id": 0,
          "block_order": 1
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "So ",
          "block_bbox": [
            167,
            526,
            281,
            592
          ],
          "block_id": 1,
          "block_order": 2
        },
        {
          "block_label": "formula",
          "block_content": "\\frac{d}{d x}\\Bigg(\\frac{u}{v}\\Bigg)=\\operatorname*{l i m}_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta(u/v)}{\\Delta x}=\\operatorname*{l i m}_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{v\\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x}-u\\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}}{v(v+\\Delta v)}",
          "block_bbox": [
            768,
            643,
            2226,
            919
          ],
          "block_id": 2,
          "block_order": 3
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "As $\\Delta x\\to0,\\Delta v\\to0$ also, because $v=g(x)$ is differentiable and therefore continuous.\n",
          "block_bbox": [
            159,
            1082,
            2721,
            1294
          ],
          "block_id": 3,
          "block_order": 4
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Thus, using the Limit Laws, we get ",
          "block_bbox": [
            164,
            1488,
            1716,
            1592
          ],
          "block_id": 4,
          "block_order": 5
        },
        {
          "block_label": "formula",
          "block_content": "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right)=\\frac{v\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x}-u\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}}{v\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}(v+\\Delta v)}=\\frac{v\\frac{du}{dx}-u\\frac{dv}{dx}}{v^2}",
          "block_bbox": [
            478,
            1709,
            2482,
            2085
          ],
          "block_id": 5,
          "block_order": 6
        },
        {
          "block_label": "number",
          "block_content": "15",
          "block_bbox": [
            2818,
            2121,
            2895,
            2181
          ],
          "block_id": 6,
          "block_order": null
        }
      ],
      "markdown": "## The Quotient Rule \n\nSo \n\n$$\\frac{d}{d x}\\Bigg(\\frac{u}{v}\\Bigg)=\\operatorname*{l i m}_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta(u/v)}{\\Delta x}=\\operatorname*{l i m}_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{v\\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x}-u\\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}}{v(v+\\Delta v)}$$\n\nAs $\\Delta x\\to0,\\Delta v\\to0$ also, because $v=g(x)$ is differentiable and therefore continuous.\n\n\n\nThus, using the Limit Laws, we get \n\n$$\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac{u}{v}\\right)=\\frac{v\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta u}{\\Delta x}-u\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}\\frac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta x}}{v\\lim\\limits_{\\Delta x\\to0}(v+\\Delta v)}=\\frac{v\\frac{du}{dx}-u\\frac{dv}{dx}}{v^2}$$",
